WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.379 --> 00:00:11.749
Rain World: Downpour is a game about reinventing
an ecosystem.

00:00:11.749 --> 00:00:16.760
About how precise changes to an environment
and the creatures within it can have an incredible

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.650
effect on a simulated biosphere.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:24.890
In the expansion, there are five new Slugcats
to play as, all of which feature not just

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:30.000
new, game-redefining abilities — but new
regions suited for those abilities, and new

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.200
creatures to test their limits.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.800
And like in the original base game, everything
runs on a unique system of procedural animation

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.469
and AI that makes this pixelated ecosystem
feel truly alive.

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:47.980
So, for this entry into the archive, we’ll
discover the hidden depths of Rain World:

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:48.980
Downpour.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:55.539
Now, let’s reshuffle the roles of this virtual
food chain...

00:00:55.539 --> 00:01:01.920
The first new Slugcat is the Gourmand, a rather
rotund creature that, at a glance, seems stuck

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.360
at the bottom of the evolutionary heap.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:10.310
For the Gourmand is unable to run as fast
or climb as far as most Slugcats.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:14.930
Even something as simple as throwing a spear
will tire them out, causing them to enter

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.010
a winded state until they can catch their
breath.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.850
In the race to survive, the adorable Gourmand
sadly doesn’t seem like they’ll cross

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.020
the finish line.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:27.540
But they have an ability that changes everything.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.890
If you hold any two items in each hand, this
clever creature will combine them to create

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.460
something new.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.100
Find yourself in a dark room?

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.829
The Gourmand can combine glowing slime mold
with a rock to create a lantern.

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:44.570
Or combine a Gunpowder Plant with a Sporepuff
to create an explosive.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:49.270
Or a Beehive with a Vulture Grub to create
a blinding flashbang.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:53.820
The sheer number of things you can make is
completely nuts, as this chart from the wiki

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:54.820
proves.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:59.890
And if you don’t have ingredients, the resourceful
Gourmand can simply cough one up at the cost

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:00.890
of one food.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:04.490
They’re the definition of ‘work smarter,
not harder.’

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:09.450
The Gourmand has other drawbacks, like how
they need a more sizable stockpile of food

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.450
to hibernate.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.960
But the more you play, the more you fall into
the Gourmand’s pattern of life.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.940
In one of the coolest tricks Downpour pulls,
you learn to think like the Slugcat you play

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:23.430
as to survive in the ecosystem.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:28.599
The Gormand’s path eventually takes them
to the new region of the Outer Expanse, a

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:32.340
lush and lively environment dotted with ancient
ruins.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:37.550
It would be paradise for a creature like the
Gourmand, but there are other new lifeforms

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:38.810
in this garden.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:44.159
Caramel Lizards are oversized, six-legged
brutes that can perform aggressive leaps to

00:02:44.159 --> 00:02:45.170
catch their prey.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:50.400
They also have the ability to spit projectiles
that can knock the Gourmand down or stick

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.850
them in place.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:56.700
Motivated by the promise of a tasty treat,
Carmel Lizards will use every weapon at their

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.760
disposal to try and catch the Gourmand.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.269
And like the creatures from the base game,
these enemies are powered almost entirely

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:10.790
by procedural animation and emergent behavior,
which makes them feel like living organisms.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:16.030
This approach is insanely cool and was also
insanely difficult to get right, according

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.760
to the developers whom I interviewed for extra
insight: Joar “Our project we set out to

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.930
do was: what if we base it entirely around
emergent behavior.”

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.099
James “We would ask ourself like: this stuff
is so cool, like, why don’t other games

00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:30.099
do this.

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:32.439
And we found out — they’re right not to
do this (laughs).”

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:36.959
Although a challenge to develop, the tech
behind creatures like the Carmel Lizards makes

00:03:36.959 --> 00:03:39.700
them engaging rivals to the Gourmand.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:44.760
But while not a master combatant, this Slugcat
has some very ‘Gourmand’ ways to handle

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:45.760
threats.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:50.030
In a pinch, they can fall from enough height
to stun enemies with their sheer bulk.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:55.190
Even better, if you give Carmel Lizards enough
of the right type of food, you can turn them

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:56.790
into your allies.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.280
For like the Gourmand, they’re fellow food-lovers.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:06.880
Unfortunately, some creatures find nothing
quite as tempting as the Gourmand themselves.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:11.900
In the humid wetlands of the Outer Expanse,
Jungle Leeches will try to latch on to the

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.129
Gourmand.

00:04:13.129 --> 00:04:17.979
These green leeches are able to stay out of
the water for long periods without drying

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:20.600
up, and slowly drain the food from their hosts.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.979
Get overwhelmed, and the Gourmand becomes
dessert.

00:04:24.979 --> 00:04:30.169
This jungle might not be the easiest environment
for the Gourmand to navigate, but the determined

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:33.380
little Slugcat will keep hauling themselves
along.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:37.800
To make traversal easier, you can get a helping
hand from the Yeeks.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:43.180
These energetic, frog-like creatures are passive
lifeforms that jump around incessantly — and

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.200
if you grab hold of one, you can greatly increase
your jumping ability.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:52.210
They especially come in handy in areas dense
with Worm Grass, which will try to pull the

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.860
Gourmand in to feed.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:05:01.410
Yeek traversal is another example of the Gourmand
using their intelligence to overcome their

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.410
shortcomings.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.510
Ultimately, the Gourmand’s journey is a
story of learning to work your way up from

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.160
the bottom of the food chain.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:12.390
And if you eat every type of food, it unlocks
an incredible piece of post-game content that

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:16.110
I’ll reveal at the end of the video.

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:21.169
But the next Slugcat, the Artificer, isn’t
interesting in the joys of life.

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:26.610
In many ways the Gourmand’s opposite, this
aggressive creature is an expert in explosives,

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:31.650
able to turn any regular spear into an explosive
one, or cough up a grenade.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:36.449
These weapons encourage an aggressive playstyle
that can result in you blowing yourself up,

00:05:36.449 --> 00:05:40.199
but fortunately, the Artificer is immune to
explosive damage.

00:05:40.199 --> 00:05:45.169
In fact, blowing themselves up is the main
way they get around, as they can create a

00:05:45.169 --> 00:05:48.490
small, midair explosion to give their jump
extra height.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:54.289
While tricky to use at first, this explosive
jump soon becomes integral to navigating the

00:05:54.289 --> 00:05:58.699
environment, and encourages you to approach
movement with the same aggressive momentum

00:05:58.699 --> 00:05:59.900
as combat.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:04.130
But like the Gourmand, the Artificer has downsides.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:08.830
Use the explosive jump too much, and you’ll
start smoking — and if you jump again, you’ll

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.319
be knocked unconscious.

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:13.150
Ignore this warning, and it’s game over.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:19.000
But while the Artificer is a danger to themselves,
they are even more dangerous to their many

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.000
enemies.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.139
For this vengeful Slugcat is hunting the most
intelligent creatures in Rain World — the

00:06:25.139 --> 00:06:26.250
Scavengers.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:30.759
In the original game, the advanced Scavenger
groups could be reasoned with, and would only

00:06:30.759 --> 00:06:32.700
attack if you caused trouble.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:37.080
But in this game, their AI’s aggression
is locked at maximum, and they’ll use their

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.740
considerable intelligence to try and take
the Artificer out.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:45.061
As you move through the game, they’ll send
out assassination squads, set up ambushes,

00:06:45.061 --> 00:06:49.620
and even unleash their ultimate weapon — Elite
Scavengers.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:55.319
An ‘eye-for-an-eye’ response to the Artificer’s
escalation, these hunters have unique masks

00:06:55.319 --> 00:06:58.120
and electrified spears that do extra damage.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:03.661
They’re also considerably more mobile, able
to leap long distances and smoke you out if

00:07:03.661 --> 00:07:05.699
you try to hide somewhere out of reach.

00:07:05.699 --> 00:07:10.360
It can really feel like you’re battling
an autonomous intelligence instead of enemies

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.599
in a video game.

00:07:11.599 --> 00:07:14.700
James “You have these AI creatures that
have their own agency, right?

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:19.789
And they have all of these various competing
impulses, I guess you’d say.”

00:07:19.789 --> 00:07:24.889
The Artificer’s path of violence eventually
leads them to the Metropolis, a crumbling

00:07:24.889 --> 00:07:30.099
ancient city you can access thanks to an ID
drone that accidently links with you.

00:07:30.099 --> 00:07:34.610
You’re here to flush out the Scavengers,
but even while you’re on the warpath, it’s

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:39.539
hard not to be moved by the beautiful environments
of this region, which tell a haunting story

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:42.039
of a civilization that vanished.

00:07:42.039 --> 00:07:48.300
In some areas, the technology still functions,
with rooms that continue to glow with holographic

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:53.470
displays, and even some low gravity chambers
home to Neuron Flies.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:58.690
These multicolored drone swarms seem to store
data, and while they might seem defenseless,

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.039
messing with them is a bad idea.

00:08:01.039 --> 00:08:04.099
For the Neuron Flies have a protector.

00:08:04.099 --> 00:08:09.419
Inspectors are bizarre, multi-headed artificial
beings programmed to defend the neuron swarm

00:08:09.419 --> 00:08:10.960
at all costs.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:16.070
If you snatch a Fly, their bodies will flash
red and they’ll go on the offensive, flinging

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:19.509
the Artificer around the room or catching
spears mid-air.

00:08:19.509 --> 00:08:24.720
And since each head seems to have their own
AI, they’re a unique challenge to outwit.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:30.240
The only way to defeat this mechanical hydra
is to destroy all three heads, after which

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.649
the Inspector will explode.

00:08:32.649 --> 00:08:37.330
It seems wherever the Artificer goes, destruction
follows.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:42.409
If you continue to blaze onwards, you will
eventually come face to face with the Chieftain

00:08:42.409 --> 00:08:47.570
Scavenger, a unique being that won’t attack
you outright, giving you a final chance to

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:48.860
turn back.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:53.589
But at this point, you see the world as the
Artificer does, and violence is likely your

00:08:53.589 --> 00:08:55.149
first instinct.

00:08:55.149 --> 00:08:59.279
If you do decide to battle the Chieftain,
you’re in for a fight more challenging than

00:08:59.279 --> 00:09:01.800
any other Scavenger you’ve faced.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:07.390
No matter the outcome, however, the Scavenger
seems stuck in an endless cycle of destruction.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:12.459
And the game does a great job pulling you
into that cycle of escalation, encouraging

00:09:12.459 --> 00:09:18.519
you to tear through the ecosystem with explosive
recklessness.

00:09:18.519 --> 00:09:23.070
Yet the middle Slugcat — the Rivulet — survives
not through strength, but agility.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:28.230
My personal favorite, the Rivulet can run
faster, climb faster, and swim faster than

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.730
a typical Slugcat.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:34.950
In fact, the Rivulet is so quick that they
can outmaneuver creatures like the Leviathan,

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:39.700
which in the base game were virtually impossible
to escape from on your own.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:45.540
And thanks to the Rivulet’s primitive gills,
they can also stay underwater for long periods.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.520
These adaptations are absolutely critical
to the Rivulet’s survival, as at this point

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:55.890
in the timeline, the rain comes so frequently
that the land has become a drowned kingdom

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:57.340
of unending floods.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:01.100
And the Rivulet’s attunement to their environment
was quite intentional:

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.390
Andrew: “They were kind of the slugcat that
originally sparked off the idea of ‘what

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:12.230
if all these new slugcats had some region
or ecosystem that ties into their abilities.”

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:17.790
Yet the Rivulet is not the only lifeform that
has adapted to this new environment.

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:22.971
Eels are aquatic hunters that slither in the
bowels of this waterlogged dominion, and seem

00:10:22.971 --> 00:10:25.090
to be an offshoot of the lizards.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:29.769
They propel their slender bodies through the
water with their long, spiny tail — the

00:10:29.769 --> 00:10:34.089
bioluminescent glow of their heads casting
an eerie light.

00:10:34.089 --> 00:10:38.980
In open waters, packs of Eels will cut the
Rivulet off from all angles.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:43.840
Their AI works a bit like the Salamanders
of the base game, if they had their reaction

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:47.089
time and mobility dialed all the way up.

00:10:47.089 --> 00:10:51.670
But there are larger and more aggressive predators
than Eels in these waters.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:56.399
Aquapedes are another major threat to the
Rivulet — huge aquatic centipedes with a

00:10:56.399 --> 00:10:58.540
bottomless appetite.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:02.740
Seemingly a relative of the flying Centiwings
that have turned their wings to flippers,

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:07.769
Aquapedes might make you think twice about
taking a swim…

00:11:07.769 --> 00:11:11.959
Yet the more you play as the Rivulet, the
more navigating the depths becomes second

00:11:11.959 --> 00:11:12.959
nature.

00:11:12.959 --> 00:11:17.870
Eventually, you gather the courage to dive
deep into the Submerged Superstructure, a

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:21.050
late game region that is almost entirely underwater.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:27.860
And in these recesses, the deadliest aquatic
predator skulks in the form of the Giant Jellyfish.

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:33.290
Occasionally spotted closer to the surface,
these gargantuan siphonophores can sense prey

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.639
through vibrations in the water.

00:11:35.639 --> 00:11:40.160
Move too much, and the Giant Jellyfish will
send out their tentacles in pursuit of the

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:45.820
Rivulet — dragging them in close and administering
a lethal electric shock from an orb-shaped

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.820
organ.

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:51.450
Yet these tentacles have a maximum range,
and if you’re well-practiced, you can lure

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:54.649
the tentacles out, then swim right under them.

00:11:54.649 --> 00:12:00.320
By the end of the Rivulet’s storyline, you
truly feel like an Olympic swimmer, and are

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:04.930
more at home in the water than on the land
— despite the abundance of predators…

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:10.860
But what about a Slugcat that doesn’t avoid
predators, but is one?

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:15.829
The Spearmaster is an at first unassuming
creature that pulls spear-like quills from

00:12:15.829 --> 00:12:16.829
its tail.

00:12:16.829 --> 00:12:22.149
When thrown, these spears can impale and drain
the life from other organisms.

00:12:22.149 --> 00:12:27.100
And since the Spearmaster is unable to eat
due to having no mouth, leeching off other

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.470
species is the only way to stay alive.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:36.070
This seemingly simple change turns the entire
game of Rain World on its head, because now,

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:41.270
instead of being constantly on the run from
carnivores, you are the carnivore, seeking

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:46.210
out other lifeforms and slowly draining them
like a tiny vampire.

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:48.389
Yet the Spearmaster is not invincible.

00:12:48.389 --> 00:12:53.940
It exists in an era long before the other
Slugcats, where competition is fierce and

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.560
predators are more numerous.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:01.500
And some predators are so dangerous, even
a biological terror like the Spearmaster needs

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:02.880
to be careful.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:08.470
Mother Spiders are huge arachnids that scuttle
in the dim corners of the region, their abdomen

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:11.279
swollen due to carrying their brood.

00:13:11.279 --> 00:13:16.430
Attack one, and a hoard of ravenous Coalescipedes
are unleashed — infant spiders that link

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:20.760
together into a centipede like formation to
attack the player.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:26.300
This protective swarm can overwhelm the Spearmaster
in seconds, which is why it is fortunate that

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:31.940
Mother Spiders will avoid confrontations — if
you keep your distance.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:35.290
But not all predators offer this courtesy.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:40.600
Stowaways are near-invisible ambush predators
that impale their prey with long, fleshy tendrils

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:45.240
— then pull them upwards towards their perch
on the ceiling, where a mouth rimmed with

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:48.149
jagged fangs swallows them whole.

00:13:48.149 --> 00:13:53.420
Battling Stowaways is exceedingly risky, as
one often doesn’t spot them until it’s

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.420
too late.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:59.009
And it’s not just the Slugcat that the Stowaway
can catch off guard, as they’ll eat anything

00:13:59.009 --> 00:14:00.779
they can drag up into their gullet.

00:14:00.779 --> 00:14:06.130
It can be hard not to feel outclassed as a
predator when dealing with such an effective

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.210
hunter.

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:11.730
And there is no hunter more effective than
the Mother Long Legs.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:17.720
A primordial ancestor of the other Long Leg
species, this artificial terror is a tentacled

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:22.660
mass that prowls the Garbage Wastes, feeding
on anything that gets stuck in its web of

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:23.660
tendrils.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:28.630
Although unable to see, the Mother Long Legs
reacts dynamically to sound, able to lock

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:31.779
on to prey if they make the slightest whisper.

00:14:31.779 --> 00:14:37.300
Yet while these terrors are virtually invincible,
if you’re careful, you can actually impale

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:41.639
the Mother Long Legs and leech off their energy
— proving that it’s not the size of the

00:14:41.639 --> 00:14:44.089
hunter that matters, but the tenacity.

00:14:44.089 --> 00:14:49.680
And the more you settle into playing as the
Spearmaster, the bolder you become — working

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:55.649
your way up the food chain until everything
feels like it’s on the menu.

00:14:55.649 --> 00:14:59.750
Yet the final Slugcat is the Spearmaster’s
spiritual opposite.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:05.050
The Saint is perhaps the most unique Slugcat
of all, because they are pacifists.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:09.710
If you try to throw a spear, the Saint will
toss it so that it spins uselessly through

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:10.710
the air.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:15.430
Try to eat another animal — even something
as small as a bug — and the Saint will become

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:18.000
sick, crawling around in a dazed state.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.980
It’s plants and fungi only for this Slugcat.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:26.420
In the brutal ecosystem of Rain World, The
Saint seems hopelessly exposed… but they

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:29.380
have a very unusual trick up their sleeve.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:34.019
Using a long, chameleon-like tongue as a grappling
hook, they can lift themselves out of reach

00:15:34.019 --> 00:15:35.670
of hungry mouths.

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:40.350
This tongue greatly increases their mobility,
allowing them to swing themselves through

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:42.550
the ruined environment they call home.

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:48.160
For the Saint lives at the absolute tail end
of Rain World’s timeline, in an era where

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:51.480
the land seems locked in a brutal ice age.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:56.760
The Rain has been replaced with unforgiving
snow storms, cloaking the desolate remains

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:00.339
of the ecosystem in a funeral shroud of white.

00:16:00.339 --> 00:16:05.380
Stay out in the cold too long and you will
slowly freeze, with the Saint becoming paler

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:08.649
and paler as their metabolism shuts down.

00:16:08.649 --> 00:16:13.509
The only way to endure this forsaken climate
is to take frequent shelter.

00:16:13.509 --> 00:16:16.569
But this ecosystem is not completely barren.

00:16:16.569 --> 00:16:22.230
The pale Strawberry Lizards trudge through
the snowstorm, managing to cling to life.

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:27.449
And like all lizards from past eras, these
ice age reptiles are predators.

00:16:27.449 --> 00:16:32.459
To catch the Saint, Strawberry Lizards have
convergently evolved the same grapple-tongue

00:16:32.459 --> 00:16:38.009
method of locomotion, making them one of the
most maneuverable and unpredictable predator

00:16:38.009 --> 00:16:40.380
species of any era.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:44.829
Using their tongue, the Lizards will fling
themselves at the Saint, grappling onto the

00:16:44.829 --> 00:16:48.350
ceiling next to them, or even onto the Saint
themselves.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:52.959
Trying to anticipate how the Lizards’ AI
will interact with the game’s physics system

00:16:52.959 --> 00:16:55.330
is exceedingly difficult, making them a worthy
rival to the agile Saint.

00:16:55.330 --> 00:17:00.430
Yet even in competition, it is hard not to
feel strangely sorry for these lizards, who

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:05.559
like you are doing all they can to survive
in this endless winter.

00:17:05.559 --> 00:17:11.870
These are creatures of the snow, focused primarily
on outlasting the cold.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:15.140
Not all creatures are interested in playing
it cool.

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:20.560
In the warm-hued region of the Rubicon — an
underground locale exclusive to the Saint’s

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:24.929
storyline — the hot-tempered Firebugs are
quick to go on the offensive.

00:17:24.929 --> 00:17:29.910
If you accidently startle one, they will quite
literally explode with anger, sending their

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:34.390
eggs scattering and careening towards the
Saint like a heat-seeking missile.

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:39.560
Not one to forget a grudge, they will continue
to pursue you until they find their target.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:44.929
It's best to behave like a saint, and give
them no reason to get aggressive.

00:17:44.929 --> 00:17:50.030
Yet the final lifeform is as needlessly aggressive
as the Saint is peaceful.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:55.650
Swooping in on massive wings, Miros Vultures
are a whirlwind of teeth and claws that give

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:57.530
a whole new meaning to death from above.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.350
A horrific amalgamation of Vultures and Miros
Birds, the Miros Vulture is relentless in

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:05.730
its path of destruction, moving through areas
like a living natural disaster.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:09.870
If their beak that can slay you in one hit
and the blades on their wings aren’t enough,

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:15.410
the Miros Vulture’s glowing eye can also
unleash a laser that explodes with concussive

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:16.429
force.

00:18:16.429 --> 00:18:21.670
But even this nightmare of a predator is often
no match for the Saint’s simple, passive

00:18:21.670 --> 00:18:22.670
avoidance.

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:27.630
You can defeat Miros Vultures the same way
you defeat the snow: by staying calm and waiting

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.380
out the storm.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:34.330
Like all the Slugcats before it, playing as
the Saint will make you think like one, approaching

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:40.830
all situations with a clear mind and avoiding
fights instead of starting them.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:45.180
Each of the five campaigns change both the
ecosystem, and the way you think about your

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.180
place in it.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:50.530
And if you fulfill all the requirements in
the Gourmand’s campaign, you unlock something

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:51.840
very special.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:57.429
The next time you boot up the game, you might
encounter a final creature — the Slugpups.

00:18:57.429 --> 00:19:02.960
These adorable infant Slugcats offer a new
way to navigate the game, because now, you

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:03.960
can be a parent.

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:07.960
And you can take them by the hand or carry
them all the way to the end.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.170
And you can adopt more than one.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:14.760
Make sure you’re ready for the extra responsibility
though, because once a pup bonds with you

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:20.030
it becomes your duty to protect them from
the dangers of Rain World, which can be extremely

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:21.030
stressful.

00:19:21.030 --> 00:19:24.030
But it’s a cool hidden system, with a surprising
amount of depth.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:28.409
Andrew “We basically has just one person
on the team just solely devoted to developing

00:19:28.409 --> 00:19:31.179
the Slugpups” James “It’s a very big
project.

00:19:31.179 --> 00:19:32.810
It’s huge!”

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:37.480
No matter how you get to the end, each of
the new Slugcats has at least one conclusion

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:41.669
that wraps up their journey in a poignant
yet unexpected way.

00:19:41.669 --> 00:19:45.780
If you’d like to check out the expansion
for yourself, once again, be aware that the

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:47.720
game is exceedingly difficult.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:53.030
I’ve never felt more aware of my vulnerable
place in a virtual ecosystem than when playing

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:57.039
Rain World — which is by design: Joar: “Rain
World is about humility, right?

00:19:57.039 --> 00:19:59.440
It’s like: you’re not some big hero, you’re
just this little creature.”

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:05.920
A tremendous thank you to the creative minds
behind this game for sharing insights into

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:08.030
how the ecosystem came together.

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:12.820
It’s been an honor exploring this pixelated
biosphere.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:15.450
As always, thanks for watching.

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:19.900
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
support by liking, subscribing, and hitting

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:24.280
the notification icon to stay up to date on
all things Curious.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:34.019
See you in the next video.

